※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4632

※ What a lambda brought in by value reaches what that value was made in.  Text
※ made in an arena of the call's own is given back with the arena on the way
※ out, so a lambda carrying it may not be answered.  A string would be copied
※ into `⎕heap` here; a lambda is never copied, what it brought in being laid out
※ the way its body reads it and nothing else knowing how.

fn greeting(name: str) → fn() → str:
    let pool: mut arena = ⎕arena
    defer ⎕empty(pool)
    let said: str = "hello " ⧺ name in pool
    λ [said] → str { said }

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    0u6
